---
// Dev-only harness for the reaction bar and comment thread. The point is the
// CONTEXT: the components render inside a real BlogLayout, a real
// .blog-article-wrap, and a real .blog-prose column, so the measure, greys,
// dark mode, and the hairline they share with .blog-end are all honest.
//
// Query params flip the states worth reviewing side by side:
//   ?state=loaded | loading | empty | error | closed   (thread)
//   ?phase=anonymous | claimed | ready         (reader standing, compose box)
//   ?receipt=submitting | posted | held | nudge | error   (compose receipt)
//   ?more=1  ?moreState=loading                (load-more cursor button)
//   ?reacted=1                                 (filled heart, xia accent)
//   ?credits=0                                 (colophon with no model credit)
//
// Own/editing/tombstone/edited comment rows are fixture data below, not query
// params — they are thread content, not a state of the box or the list.
//
// Delete once /blog/[slug] carries the real thing.
import BlogLayout from '@/layouts/BlogLayout.astro';
import TableOfContents from '@/features/posts/ui/TableOfContents.astro';
import ReadingTopbar from '@/features/posts/ui/ReadingTopbar.astro';
import BackToTop from '@/features/posts/ui/BackToTop.astro';
import Footer from '@/features/home/ui/Footer.astro';
import ReactionBar from '@/features/comments/ui/ReactionBar';
import CommentsSection from '@/features/comments/ui/CommentsSection.astro';
import SubscribePanel from '@/features/notify/SubscribePanel.astro';
import Colophon from '@/features/posts/ui/Colophon.astro';
import ShareRow from '@/features/posts/ui/ShareRow.astro';
import { blog } from '@/data/site';
import { commentsCopy } from '@/features/comments/copy';
import { resolveAuthorshipModel } from '@/data/authorship';
import type { AuthorshipCredit } from '@/features/posts/server/directives/authors';
import type { BlogComment, ClaimedIdentity, ComposeReceipt, ReaderPhase, Viewer } from '@/features/comments/types';
import '@/features/comments/styles/comments.css';

export const prerender = false;
if (!import.meta.env.DEV) return new Response(null, { status: 404 });

const params = Astro.url.searchParams;

const rawState = params.get('state');
const state =
  rawState === 'loading' || rawState === 'empty' || rawState === 'error' || rawState === 'closed'
    ? rawState
    : 'loaded';

const rawPhase = params.get('phase');
const phase: ReaderPhase = rawPhase === 'claimed' || rawPhase === 'ready' ? rawPhase : 'anonymous';

const rawReceipt = params.get('receipt');
const receipt: ComposeReceipt =
  rawReceipt === 'submitting' || rawReceipt === 'posted' || rawReceipt === 'held'
  || rawReceipt === 'nudge' || rawReceipt === 'error'
    ? rawReceipt
    : 'idle';

const hasMore = params.get('more') === '1';
const loadMoreState = params.get('moreState') === 'loading' ? 'loading' : 'idle';
const reacted = params.get('reacted') === '1';

const viewer: Viewer = { name: 'Tutu Xiao' };
const claimed: ClaimedIdentity = { name: 'Murray', email: 'murray@example.com' };
const draftText = "Might be worth mentioning the rollback plan too — did you keep one on standby, or was cutting it part of the point?";

// Real faces on purpose: a stack of five identical initial-circles reads as one
// grey mass, which is a property of the fixture, not of the design. The shipped
// bar serves reader avatars through the signed static proxy.
const reactors = [
  { name: 'Nina Kato', avatar: 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1?s=96' },
  { name: 'Wei Zhang', avatar: 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/810438?s=96' },
  { name: 'Oskar Lind', avatar: 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124599?s=96' },
  { name: 'Priya R', avatar: 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1024025?s=96' },
  { name: 'Tom Beck' },
];

// Nearly every post credits a model, so the harness renders one: the colophon
// has to be judged with its provenance line present, not in the rare state.
// `?credits=0` shows the creditless post.
const showCredits = params.get('credits') !== '0';
const creditModel = resolveAuthorshipModel('anthropic/claude-opus-4-6');
const authorshipCredits: AuthorshipCredit[] =
  showCredits && creditModel
    ? [{ model: creditModel, note: '读了三版草稿，指出第二节在重复第一节' }]
    : [];

const editWindowSoon = Date.now() + 8 * 60 * 1000 + 24 * 1000; // ~8:24 left, for the countdown

// Fixture timestamps come off the same table the thread does, so the page is
// readable in one language at a time. Hardcoded strings left the rows dated in
// Chinese while every label around them was English, which is exactly the kind
// of drift this page exists to catch.
const t = commentsCopy[blog.locale.blog];

const comments: BlogComment[] = [
  {
    id: '1',
    author: 'Nina Kato',
    date: t.relativeDate.days(2),
    text: '这段关于"删掉一层抽象比加一层更难"的说法很准。我们上个季度做的事情几乎一模一样，最后省下来的不是代码行数，是每次改动前要读的东西。',
    likes: 7,
  },
  {
    id: '2',
    author: 'Murray',
    date: t.relativeDate.days(2),
    text: 'Exactly that. The line count barely moved — what changed is how much you have to hold in your head before you can touch it.',
    byAuthor: true,
    isReply: true,
    likes: 12,
    liked: true,
  },
  {
    id: '3',
    author: 'Oskar Lind',
    date: t.relativeDate.days(5),
    text: 'Curious whether you kept the adapter around for the migration window or cut it in one go. The one-go version always sounds cleaner than it turns out to be.',
    likes: 2,
    edited: true,
  },
  {
    id: '4',
    author: 'You',
    date: t.relativeDate.now,
    text: 'Second this — a migration window with two live paths is where most of the cost hides.',
    held: true,
    own: true,
  },
  // Tombstone: the root is gone but the reply under it stays put — one-level
  // threading has nowhere else to hang it.
  {
    id: '5',
    author: 'Deleted',
    date: t.relativeDate.days(4),
    text: '',
    tombstone: true,
  },
  {
    id: '6',
    author: 'Priya R',
    date: t.relativeDate.days(4),
    text: "Following up on that anyway — the rollback plan is the part I'd want written down before I tried this on our stack.",
    isReply: true,
    likes: 1,
  },
  // Own, still inside the 15-minute edit window — Edit is live and counting
  // down; Delete always is.
  {
    id: '7',
    author: 'Tutu Xiao',
    date: t.relativeDate.now,
    text: 'One more thing: the retry policy move is the part I keep pointing people to when this comes up internally.',
    own: true,
    editDeadline: editWindowSoon,
    likes: 3,
  },
  // Own, already mid-edit — the inline textarea swap, on screen without a
  // click.
  {
    id: '8',
    author: 'Tutu Xiao',
    date: t.relativeDate.hours(1),
    text: 'Typo in my last one — meant the retry policy, not the retry budget.',
    own: true,
    editing: true,
    editDeadline: Date.now() + 3 * 60 * 1000,
    likes: 0,
  },
  // The whole of the Markdown a comment supports, in one row -- see
  // comment-markdown.ts for why the list stops where it does. This page is
  // the only place the six constructs can be seen next to each other, and
  // the only place the server renderer is exercised at all.
  {
    id: '9',
    author: 'Wren',
    date: t.relativeDate.days(6),
    text: [
      'The **retry budget** and the *retry policy* are different things, and `maxAttempts` is',
      'only the first one. Worth splitting in the post:',
      '',
      '- budget: how much total delay a request may spend',
      '- policy: which failures are worth another try',
      '',
      '> a retry that was never going to succeed is a slower failure',
      '',
      '```',
      'if (!retryable(err)) throw err;',
      '```',
      '',
      'Context in [the AWS write-up](https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/timeouts-retries-and-backoff-with-jitter/).',
    ].join('\n'),
    likes: 4,
  },
];
---

<BlogLayout title="Lab — reactions & comments" path="/lab/comments" description="Dev harness">
  <ReadingTopbar slot="readingbar" />
  <a class="blog-back" href="/blog">{blog.copy[blog.locale.blog].back.index}</a>

  <div class="blog-article-wrap">
    <aside class="blog-aside">
      <div class="blog-aside__sticky">
        <a class="blog-back-rail" href="/blog">{blog.copy[blog.locale.blog].back.rail}</a>
        <TableOfContents />
      </div>
    </aside>

    <article>
      <header class="blog-article__header">
        <h1 class="blog-article__title">少一层，而不是多一层</h1>
        <div class="blog-article__meta">
          <span>Murray</span>
          <span>2026年8月20日</span>
          <span>6分钟</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="blog-prose">
        <p>
          去年冬天我们决定把一整层抽象删掉。那层东西存在了两年半，谁也说不清它当初解决了什么问题——
          只知道每次改动都要先穿过它，再从另一头出来。
        </p>

        <h2>先说结论</h2>
        <p>
          删掉之后代码行数只少了 <code>1,800</code> 行，占整个仓库不到百分之三。
          真正变化的不是体积，是每次动手之前需要装进脑子里的东西。
          这件事没有任何一张图表能表现出来，但每个人都感觉到了。
        </p>
        <p>
          我一直觉得，判断一个抽象好不好，不看它省了多少代码，而看它
          <a href="#">让你不需要知道多少东西</a>。省代码的抽象很多，
          真正减少认知负担的很少。
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>
            一层抽象如果没有让调用它的人少知道一些事，那它只是把复杂度换了个地方放。
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <h3>那两年半它做了什么</h3>
        <p>
          它包了三个 API，统一了错误格式，还顺手做了重试。听起来都对。
          问题是这三件事根本不需要在同一层里做，而且它们各自的生命周期完全不同：
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>错误格式一年动一次；</li>
          <li>重试策略每次事故之后都要改；</li>
          <li>三个 API 里有两个在第二年就下线了。</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          于是每次调重试参数，都要碰一个还在给两个死掉的 API 做兼容的文件。
          这就是那种最难察觉的成本——它不表现为 bug，只表现为犹豫。
        </p>

        <h2>拆的过程</h2>
        <p>
          最开始想的是留一个适配层过渡，两条路并行跑一个月。写到一半发现，
          维护两条活着的路径本身比一次切干净贵得多，而且贵在人身上不是机器上。
        </p>
        <pre><code>// before: one door, three unrelated jobs behind it
await gateway.call('billing.invoice', payload)

// after: the retry policy is where the failure is
await billing.invoice(payload)</code></pre>
        <p>
          最后是在一个周三下午一次性切的。回滚方案准备了，没用上。
          事后复盘时有人说，如果当初那层从来没建过，我们大概会更早发现三个 API 里有两个没人用。
        </p>

        <h3>留下来的判断</h3>
        <p>
          现在再有人提议加一层，我会先问一个问题：加完之后，用它的人可以
          <strong>不知道</strong>什么？如果答案是"没有，只是写起来短一点"，
          那它不是抽象，是缩写。
        </p>
        <p>
          缩写也有价值，但它不该用抽象的价格买。
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* The real components, not stand-ins: the colophon sits directly above
          the comments head, and the only way to judge that seam is to render
          both sides of it for real. */}
      <Colophon credits={authorshipCredits}>
        <ReactionBar client:idle count={24} reacted={reacted} reactors={reactors} locale={blog.locale.blog} />
        <div class="blog-article-sub">
          <SubscribePanel variant="blog" anchor="right" feed={blog.feed} />
          <ShareRow title="少一层，而不是多一层" />
        </div>
      </Colophon>

      <CommentsSection
        comments={comments}
        state={state}
        phase={phase}
        viewer={viewer}
        claimed={claimed}
        receipt={receipt}
        draftText={draftText}
        hasMore={hasMore}
        loadMoreState={loadMoreState}
      />
    </article>
  </div>

  <footer class="blog-end">
    <span class="blog-comment__date">Prev / next sits here</span>
  </footer>


  <Footer />
  <BackToTop />
</BlogLayout>
